{"type":"message","id":"6534f5eb","parentId":"ad3fa0bd","timestamp":"2026-04-01T10:05:31.465Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is saying they want to organize the e-books in the \"F盘里面的那个电子书文件夹\" - the e-books folder on F drive. They said \"就只是那个\" which means \"just that one\" - referring to a specific folder.\n\nLet me find the actual e-books folder. Looking at the earlier scan, the actual e-books might be in a folder with Chinese name that shows as \"电子书\" or similar. Let me scan for actual directories on F drive that might be the e-books folder. From the earlier listing, I didn't see an obvious \"电子书\" folder. Let me check more carefully.\n\nWait - the user said \"F盘里面的那个电子书文件夹\" - maybe there's a specific folder that contains e-books. Let me look at the scan results again. The folder \"x300pro\" seems to contain \"文档文件\" with study materials. The \"idm下载\" folder has mostly game mod files. The \"sa\" folder has art teacher recruitment exam papers.\n \nHold on - the first scan output was showing garbled Chinese characters, so I need to scan F drive again with UTF-8 encoding to see the actual folder names clearly.","thinkingSignature":"8000e0059b508c25d61cd52cb81f70747d8180d6757a22c88ae48f3ef63e4d91"},{"type":"text","text":"让我重新扫描 F 盘，找出那个电子书文件夹。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_umrm65jg6nb7_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"[Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; Get-ChildItem -Path \"F:\\\" -Directory -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":77,"output":325,"cacheRead":100891,"cacheWrite":3208,"totalTokens":104501,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775037920532,"responseId":"061c20df47dca5da8cecf5b308dd8d0e"}}
