{"type":"message","id":"6f2ebc66","parentId":"17f55e0d","timestamp":"2026-04-01T11:05:29.594Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants option B - full reclassification. This is a massive amount of files. Let me think about a sensible classification structure.\n\nBased on the files, the user is studying Visual Communication/Design (视觉传达). The files span 大二下 and 大三上/下. Let me think about what categories make sense:\n\n**By Course Type:**\n1. **摄影课** - Photography courses (raw files, edited photos, studio shots)\n2. **设计作业** - Design work (VI, brand, poster, font)\n3. **视频作业** - Video/AE/PR work\n4. **建模/3D** - 3D modeling (Blender, C4D)\n\n\n5. **文档/论文** - Documents, reports, papers\n6. **素材** - Reference materials\n7. **勤工俭学** - Work-study files\n8. **电子书/文献** - E-books and academic references\n9. **工程文件** - Source files (PSD, AI, etc.)\n10. **课程作业汇总** - Sorted by semester and course\n\nThis is going to be complex. I should write a PowerShell script to handle the reorganization, but the user needs to confirm they want to proceed since moving thousands of files could cause issues if the structure isn't right.\n\nLooking at what I'm working with, the main folders are 大二下 and 大三上/下, with nested subfolders for different subjects like photography, design work, videos, models, documents, and references. The大二下 folder alone has tons of RAW photos organized into categories like studio shots and outdoor photography, plus design work files and various documents about marketing and surveys.\n\nFor 大三上, I'm seeing course materials for creative thinking, work-study programs, printing assignments, brand planning projects, and a large collection of reference images, along with some animation exercises in CLIP format.\n\nLooking at the rest of the folders, there's substantial 3D modeling practice files in both 大三上 and 大三下 using Blender, design work for cultural creative products and packaging, plus course-related documents like internship reports and graduation papers. There's also some design-related PDFs and font references scattered throughout, and I notice the folder structure continues into other directories outside the main academic year folders.\n\nThe key decision is whether to reorganize by course type while keeping semester information as a secondary grouping, or to reorganize by semester first. Given the scope of what the user is asking for—hundreds of files across multiple categories—I should write a comprehensive PowerShell script that can handle this systematic reorganization. The main challenge is that the current folder names are already fairly well-organized by course, so I need to clarify the target structure before executing anything that moves files around. for a full reorganization. Let me think about what the final structure should look like. The user's a design student with files spanning two semesters, so I should organize everything by course type while preserving the semester context. I'm sketching out a folder hierarchy starting with大三 courses like VI design projects and brand planning, then大二 courses with photography and design foundations, plus a shared resources section for fonts and templates, and separate folders for work-study files and course documents.\n\nThis is going to be a complex operation with hundreds of files to move, and I'm particularly worried about the RAW files from photography—that's thousands of files across dozens of subfolders that could easily break references or get corrupted during reorganization. I need to be careful and maybe suggest doing this in stages rather than all at once.\n\nActually, looking at the scope more carefully, the RAW files alone number in the thousands, plus hundreds of other items. Before I commit to moving everything, I should clarify whether the user wants me to reorganize the existing folders in place or create an entirely new parallel structure. And I need to make sure they understand the risk involved so they can decide if they want to proceed or break this into smaller chunks.\n\nFor the reorganization itself, I'm thinking a top-level structure organized by course type makes the most sense, with subcategories for things like photography (keeping the studio/outdoor/raw/processed hierarchy intact), design work, video projects, 3D modeling, documents, and reference materials. Within each of those, I can organize by semester or topic depending on what makes sense for that particular subject.\n\nThe main thing I need to clarify before executing is whether the user wants this moved to a completely new folder structure, or if they want me to reorganize the existing folders in place. Since they're asking me to just do it, I think proceeding with a full reorganization under a new parent folder is the right call, but I should present the plan first so they can confirm before I start moving hundreds of files around.","thinkingSignature":"77006ff457f12dd458e27cce1e675fc5bcd3cdfc09f6a4a145f760e7b66adb4b"},{"type":"text","text":"好，这个工作量比较大，涉及大二、大三上下三个学期数千个文件。在开始移动之前，先确认一下整理方案：\n\n---\n\n**建议的新目录结构：**\n\n```\nD:\\贵阳人文科技学院\\\n├── 📷 摄影课/\n│   ├── 大二下/           ← 原\"大二下\\摄影课所有\"\n│   │   ├── 原片(RAW)/   ← .CR2 文件\n│   │   ├── 精修/        ← 已处理.jpg/.psd\n│   │   ├── 悬浮/        ← 悬浮摄影\n│   │   ├── 户外/         ← 户外拍摄\n│   │   ├── 摄影棚/       ← 棚拍\n│   │   └── 备选/\n│   └── 参考图/           ← 平时收集的摄影参考\n│\n├── 🎬 视频与动效/\n│   ├── 大二下/           ← PR作业、AE自动保存文件\n│   └── 大三上/           ← csp动画练习、视频作业\n│\n├── 🎨 设计作品/\n│   ├── 大二下/           ← 字体作业、VI设计、工程文件(AI/PSD)\n│   ├── 大三上/           ← VI设计、品牌策划、海报、包装\n│   └── 大三下/           ← 包装设计\n│\n├── 📦 3D建模/\n│   ├── Blender/          ← .blend 文件（建模练习）\n│   └── C4D/              ← .c4d 文件\n│\n├── 📚 文档与论文/\n│   ├── 大二下/           ← 调查报告、课程作业文档\n│   ├── 大三下/           ← 实习报告、毕业论文表格\n│   └── 勤工俭学/         ← 勤工助学相关文件\n│\n├── 📖 设计文献/\n│   ├── 电子书/           ← PDF/EPUB设计书籍\n│   └── 参考资料/         ← 期刊论文、设计参考\n│\n├── 🗂️ 素材/\n│   ├── 大二下/\n│   └── 大三上/\n│\n└── 📁 项目文件/\n    ├── 绣韵水语文创VI/\n    └── 黔之南餐饮VI/\n```\n\n---\n\n**确认问题：**\n\n1. **是否按此方案执行？** 还是你有其他想法？\n2. **大三上 \"大三上\\勤工俭学文件件\"** 要单独归类还是保留原状？\n\n方案确认后我开始执行。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":1468,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":94757,"totalTokens":126768,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775041476765,"responseId":"061c2ec4744fdeabecda588b2bbc3c57"}}
