{"type":"message","id":"5864286b","parentId":"f0b716fe","timestamp":"2026-04-01T11:42:24.183Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to send a message to their WeChat contact \"林子涵\" from OpenClaw. The message content is \"由openclaw发出\". \n\nBut I need to be careful here - the user previously said \"你给我发这条消息是由openclaw发出\" which means \"send this message as from OpenClaw\". However, sending messages on WeChat through OpenClaw requires the openclaw-weixin plugin to be properly configured with message sending capabilities.\n\nLet me check if the message tool supports WeChat messaging. Looking at the message tool description:\n- For `action=send`, include `to` and `message`.\n- If multiple channels are configured, pass `channel` (telegram|whatsapp|discord|irc|googlechat|slack|signal|imessage|line|feishu|openclaw-weixin).\n\n\n- If I use `message` with `channel=openclaw-weixin` and `to=林子涵`, it should route to that WeChat contact.\n\nThe tricky part is that WeChat is personal and private, so I need to be certain about how to address the recipient correctly - likely using theWeixin ID format like `xxx@im.wechat` that appears in the current chat metadata.\n\nI should attempt to send the message using the message tool rather than asking the user to confirm, since they've already given permission and specified the content. If the openclaw-weixin plugin doesn't support this or the routing fails, I'll let them know.","thinkingSignature":"80e36f265964ca1aca377af82c3acfb1a4a9cdec6b98ff376d0a97d2e6a4b10c"},{"type":"text","text":"\n好的，我用 message 工具发送。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_uzenkdt2fomd_1","name":"message","arguments":{"action":"send","channel":"openclaw-weixin","target":"林子涵","message":"由openclaw发出"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":377,"cacheRead":33214,"cacheWrite":122,"totalTokens":33840,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,