{"type":"message","id":"003769e0","parentId":"20cc712c","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:25:49.098Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to collect news from Reuters tomorrow morning at 7:30. This sounds like they want me to set up a scheduled task/cron job to fetch Reuters news at 7:30 AM. But wait, I'm not sure if they mean:\n\n1. A one-time reminder/scheduled task to fetch news tomorrow morning at 7:30\n2. Or they want me to just remember to do it\n\nSince I don't have a cron job feature built-in per se, but I do have the ability to set up cron jobs via the HEARTBEAT.md mechanism or by using the session spawning feature. However, this is a specific one-time task at a specific time tomorrow.\n \nI think the simplest approach is to set a cron job that runs once tomorrow at 7:30 AM to fetch Reuters news and deliver it through the WeChat channel. Since it's openclaw-weixin, I need to figure out how to format the delivery properly—I'll need to include the channel and account ID parameters in the cron job setup.","thinkingSignature":"86c74bfc631f871ed46bf57e032a076957a918026fa57dd0eb0d3ea27c329c56"},{"type":"text","text":"好的，我帮你设置一个定时任务，明天早上7:30自动采集路透社新闻发给你。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8bqxfes5vic3_1","name":"message","arguments":{"action":"send","channel":"openclaw-weixin","accountId":"0aec9dc831ba-im-bot","message":"明天7:30采集路透社新闻","silent":true,"target":"zhangqf"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":330,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":97065,"totalTokens":97522,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775060735008,"responseId":"061c79ffd2087b20444700fd4525c22e"}}
