{"type":"message","id":"a8271cbb","parentId":"10aad7df","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:26:09.636Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that I need to know the user's WeChat ID. Let me think about this - the user said \"给我采集路透社的新闻\" - they want me to collect Reuters news and send it to them. \n\nI should set up a cron job that fires at 7:30 AM tomorrow. For the WeChat channel, I need to set `delivery.target` to the current user's WeChat ID and `delivery.channel` to `openclaw-weixin`.\n\nBut I don't know the user's WeChat ID. The current inbound context shows:\n- chat_id: \"o9cq80-kvf4nL4624xk10pdRgbnM@im.wechat\"\n- account_id: \"0aec9dc831ba-im-bot\"\n- channel: \"openclaw-weixin\"\n\nThe chat_id seems to be the user's WeChat ID. Let me try to set up a cron with that.\n\nActually, looking at the documentation again for cron job delivery:\n```\nIMPORTANT: When creating a cron job for the current Weixin user, you MUST set delivery.to to the user's Weixin ID (the xxx@im.wechat address from the current conversation) AND set delivery.accountId to the current AccountId. Without an explicit 'to', the cron delivery will fail with 'requires target'. Without an explicit 'accountId', the message may be sent from the wrong bot account.\n```\n\nSo I need to use `delivery.to` = the WeChat ID from the current conversation context.\n\nThe current chat_id from the inbound meta is: `o9cq80-kvf4nL4624xk10pdRgbnM@im.wechat`\n\nBut I'm not sure if that's the right format for `delivery.to`. Let me try.\n\nActually, I realize I might be overcomplicating this. The user said \"明天早上七点半给我采集路透社的新闻\" - they want me to collect Reuters news tomorrow morning at 7:30. This is a one-time task. But I don't have a built-in cron system in this context.\n\nWait, actually looking at the AGENTS.md and system instructions, there's mention of cron jobs. Let me re-read.\n\nFrom AGENTS.md:\n\"### Heartbeat vs Cron: When to Use Each\n**Use cron when:**\n- Exact timing matters ('9:00 AM sharp every Monday')\n- Task needs isolation from main session history\n- One-shot reminders ('remind me in 20 minutes')\"\n\nSo I can create a cron job. But I need to figure out the right syntax. Let me try spawning a subagent with a delay, or creating a proper cron event.\n\nActually, I think the simplest approach is to just tell the user I'll do it tomorrow morning. But that requires me to be running and remembering. Since I don't have persistent memory between sessions (except files), I should probably set up a cron job.\n\nLet me try using the exec tool to set up a at/schtasks command for Windows to run a script at 7:30 tomorrow. Or I could use a PowerShell script.\n\nActually, I think the cleanest way is to set up a cron event through the system. Let me just tell the user \"好的，明天7:30我会采集路透社新闻发给你\" and see if that works. If the system has cron capability, it should handle it.\n\nBut actually, I'm not sure if I can create cron jobs through this interface. Let me try a different approach - maybe I can use the browser to open Reuters and take a snapshot at the scheduled time, or maybe I should just respond to the user that I'll handle it in tomorrow's session.\n\nThe most straightforward approach is to set up a Windows scheduled task using schtasks to run a script that fetches Reuters headlines and sends them via the message tool tomorrow morning at 7:30.","thinkingSignature":"374c3f55207df2426d469a504b5ef8cae74bb3202180dd37d7d55116b6b5c94e"},{"type":"text","text":"好的，我帮你设置定时任务。稍等一下，我来创建一个定时脚本。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_annl3yfwp6zr_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"Get-Date\" && whoami"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":67154,"output":831,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98401,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775060749126,"responseId":"061c7a0d7a1fb