{"type":"message","id":"095ea2ab","parentId":"1dbf456c","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:26:32.840Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the current date/time is April 2, 2026 00:26. The user wants news at 7:30 AM on April 2, 2026 (tomorrow, but it's already April 2 so \"tomorrow\" would be April 3). Actually it's currently April 2 00:26, so 7:30 AM today is in about 7 hours. Let me re-read the request.\n\n\"明天早上七点半给我采集路透社的新闻\"\n\nCurrent time is April 2 00:26. \"明天早上七点半\" would be April 3, 2026 7:30 AM.\n\nLet me create a scheduled task for 7:30 AM tomorrow (April 3). I'll create a PowerShell script that:\n1. Fetches Reuters news\n2. Sends it via the message tool\n\nActually, the simplest approach is to just tell the user \"好的，明天早上7:30我会给你发路透社新闻\" and then tomorrow when I receive a heartbeat or any message, I can fetch the news and send it. But that depends on me being active.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The user wants me to collect Reuters news at 7:30 AM and send it to them. I should set up a Windows scheduled task that runs a script at that time.\n\nThe script would need to:\n1. Fetch Reuters news (using curl/wget to a news API or website)\n2. Send via message tool\n\nBut I don't have a way to run the message tool from a standalone script easily. Let me think...\n\nActually, the better approach is to set up a cron job within the OpenClaw system. Looking at the docs, there's mention of cron scheduling. But I don't have explicit cron job creation tools mentioned in my function list.\n\nLet me just create a Windows scheduled task that runs a PowerShell script at 7:30 AM tomorrow. The script will:\n1. Use Invoke-WebRequest to fetch Reuters\n2. Extract headlines\n3. Save to a file or send directly\n\nActually, the simplest approach: I'll create a scheduled task that opens a URL at 7:30 AM tomorrow. But that would just open the browser, not send the content to the user.\n\nWait - I should think about this differently. When the user says \"给我采集路透社的新闻\" - are they expecting me to actively fetch and send the news, or just a reminder? Given the context of this conversation where I've been helping with various tasks, they probably want me to actually gather the news and deliver it.\n\nThe most practical solution is to set up a Windows scheduled task running a PowerShell script that fetches Reuters RSS feeds, extracts the latest headlines, formats them, and saves to a file I can reference, or even sends directly via email or a webhook if that's configured.\n\nActually, thinking about this more - I'm probably overcomplicating it. Since the user is chatting with me through WeChat and I've been responding, they likely expect me to either be available at 7:30 AM tomorrow to fetch and send the news, or to set up some automated system. Given the constraints of what I can actually do here, I should probably just acknowledge the request and explain the limitation - I can try to set up an automated task, but without a proper cron system or external automation, I'm constrained by whether I'm actually running and able to execute at that specific time.\n\nLet me just try setting up a Windows scheduled task anyway and see what happens.","thinkingSignature":"230a918b0f16e97dc708959dc9ad50f3a85af7fe79692172a0d2bd0c261c0f3c"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9c3q8l6uak73_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"whoami"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":68163,"output":747,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":99326,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775060773211,"responseId":"061c7a25a18ef61daba7f598aff51b19"}}
