{"type":"message","id":"5c6a56ff","parentId":"c2966898","timestamp":"2026-04-01T16:58:30.749Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to:\n1. Log into zlibrary with the provided credentials\n2. Download 10 books every day\n3. Save them to F:\\电子书\n\nLet me first try to access the website and understand its structure. I should use the browser to log in and then figure out how to download books. \n\nHowever, I should be careful - this is asking me to use credentials that were shared in the conversation. While these seem to be the user's own credentials for a public site, I should proceed carefully and not store or misuse these credentials.\n\nLet me use the browser to access the site and log in, then see what I can do. I'll need to explore the zlibrary interface to understand how to download books.\n\nOne concern: Z-Library is a site that has been associated with pirated content. I should be thoughtful about this - but the user is asking me to download books they already have access to, presumably for their personal use. I'll proceed cautiously and help them, but I should be aware this could involve copyrighted content.","thinkingSignature":"85137da4e82c6d82d72892257c98627adf75f271c056845f1dd4774d8c4da826"},{"type":"text","text":"我来帮你设置。先登录网站看看界面和下载流程。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0ne40kax2h08_1","name":"browser","arguments":{"action":"open","targetUrl":"https://zh.z-library.sk/?ts=1712"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":271,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":98584,"totalTokens":98982,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775062697774,"responseId":"061c81aaecb270475fadaea30b40ceb6"}}
