{"type":"message","id":"2e280d77","parentId":"906cb6fb","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:10:20.151Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_x03hod4l4t9j_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Name                                  LastWriteTime    \r\n----                                  -------------    \r\nQClaw-Setup-0.2.0-5001-336.exe        2026/4/1 17:04:48\r\nClawX-0.3.3-win-x64.exe               2026/4/1 17:04:47\r\nOpenClaw.Manager_0.0.11_x64-setup.exe 2026/4/1 16:19:11\r\nOpenClaw-Setup-0.5.0.exe              2026/4/1 16:19:11\r\nOpenClaw-Deploy-v2.0.0-setup-x64.exe  2026/4/1 16:19:09\r\n��ʦ�ʸ��϶������.pdf                2026/4/1 13:18:43"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":400,"aggregated":"Name                                  LastWriteTime    \r\n----                                  -------------    \r\nQClaw-Setup-0.2.0-5001-336.exe        2026/4/1 17:04:48\r\nClawX-0.3.3-win-x64.exe               2026/4/1 17:04:47\r\nOpenClaw.Manager_0.0.11_x64-setup.exe 2026/4/1 16:19:11\r\nOpenClaw-Setup-0.5.0.exe              2026/4/1 16:19:11\r\nOpenClaw-Deploy-v2.0.0-setup-x64.exe  2026/4/1 16:19:09\r\n��ʦ�ʸ��϶������.pdf                2026/4/1 13:18:43","cwd":"C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775063420148}}
{"type":"message","id":"ab89486d","parentId":"2e280d77","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:10:39.179Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the Downloads folder has some files but no new books from Z-Library. The files there are:\n1. QClaw-Setup-0.2.0-5001-336.exe\n2. ClawX-0.3.3-win-x64.exe\n3. OpenClaw.Manager_0.0.11_x64-setup.exe\n4. OpenClaw-Setup-0.5.0.exe\n5. OpenClaw-Deploy-v2.0.0-setup-x64.exe\n6. 研究生论文模板.pdf\n\nNo ebook files from Z-Library. The issue is that when I click download, the book is marked as \"已下载\" in my library but doesn't actually download to the Downloads folder automatically. This is because the user needs to actually click the download link and the browser needs to trigger the download.\n\nLet me try clicking on the download link for a book that isn't already downloaded. Let me look for a different history book that isn't marked as \"已下载\".\n\nActually, I realize the problem - when I click download links, the browser handles the download but the file doesn't appear in the Downloads folder. This might be because:\n1. The download link requires authentication (user is logged in)\n2. The file is being downloaded but saved somewhere else\n3. The download is handled by JavaScript/AJAX which my browser automation can't fully capture\n\nLet me be honest with the user about the limitations.\n\nActually, wait - looking at the page more carefully, I see the download link is just a regular URL `/dl/aZ6m8Dzkw4`. When I click it, the browser should trigger a download. But since the file isn't appearing in the Downloads folder, it's possible that:\n\n\n1. The browser's download location is set to somewhere else\n2. The download is being blocked\n3. The file is very small (240 KB for 长安的荔枝) and maybe it downloaded somewhere\n\nLet me check if there are any recent files in the Downloads folder that might be the book.","thinkingSignature":"b2f4ea53f3f41b9164367ac269460f8dc2ef4aa3d5636e6daf1c7e759417d775"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_hpg2fyg1v20a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"Get-ChildItem 'C:\\Users\\zhang\\Downloads' -File | Where-Object { $_.LastWriteTime -gt (Get-Date).AddHours(-1) } | Select-Object Name, Length, LastWriteTime\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":128150,"output":498,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":159064,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775063420153,"responseId":"061c847c5ff603ef36e7dc2bc8494160"}}
