{"type":"message","id":"d1376b61","parentId":"dcf93613","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:12:28.079Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The downloads aren't showing up in the standard location. Maybe the browser is saving to a different location, or the file hasn't been saved yet. The error message \"Download is starting\" suggests the browser is handling the download but it might be going to a temporary location or the default browser download folder.\n\nLet me try a different approach - I'll set the browser's download directory to F:\\电子书. But I don't think I can do that programmatically.\n\nActually, the issue is that the browser is downloading to the system default, which I can't easily determine from here. The OpenClaw browser might be saving to a temp directory.\n\nLet me just be honest with the user - I've tried multiple approaches but the downloads are going to the browser's default download folder, which I can't easily redirect to F:\\电子书 without their intervention.\n\nThe most practical suggestion is:\n1. Set Chrome/Edge default download folder to F:\\电子书\n2. Then I can click downloads through the browser\n\nLet me try one more thing - navigate directly and see if the download folder is different.","thinkingSignature":"e8bca1b91889edd5d5de3bc1ab793c0c65e8f2a8a2e2795f5f189e719015a95d"},{"type":"text","text":"下载已触发，但文件保存到了浏览器默认下载目录。我没办法自动指定保存到 F:\\电子书。\n\n**最实用的方法：** 你在浏览器里设置下载路径\n\n让我帮你弄一下。你用的是 Chrome 还是 Edge？我帮你设置：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qnh8uxy5t74b_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"powershell -Command \"Get-ChildItem 'HKCU:\\Software\\Google\\Chrome' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":118770,"output":312,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":149498,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775063538036,"respons