{"type":"message","id":"727a1b59","parentId":"6e98272c","timestamp":"2026-04-01T17:21:47.012Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There seems to be encoding issues with PowerShell in the console. Let me try a simpler approach - use robocopy to move the folders, which handles Chinese characters better. I know the approximate folder names from what I saw earlier:\n\nFrom the dir /x output, I can see the short names (8.3 format). Let me try using robocopy /MOVE which should work better with non-ASCII names.Let me try using robocopy to move folders. I'll use robocopy with /MOVE /E to move the contents.Actually, let me try a different approach. I'll use cmd.exe with chcp 65001 to set UTF-8 encoding, and then use robocopy.","thinkingSignature":"1f4690032da62e56c06c49f88c923738a11b18252bc5c659cf48ecbe39d0b5bf"},{"type":"text","text":"编码有点问题，让我换个方法，用 robocopy 移动文件夹：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9dcyc3suf1kd_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"robocopy \"F:\\BaiduNetdiskDownload\" \"F:\\下载管理\\BaiduNetdiskDownload\" /MOVE /E","yieldMs":60000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":131565,"output":228,"cacheRead":30416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":162209,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775064095600,"responseId":"061c871f52bb6016807d583acee1df43"}}
