 journey from garage to tech titan\n        - paragraph: In early 1976 in California, Steve Wozniak had just completed the design of a computer circuit board he intended to share with fellow hobbyists at a prominent local club. His friend Steve Jobs also saw a business opportunity to manufacture and sell the boards, and thus Apple was born.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e31] [nth=1]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 14 hours ago\n        - link \"Ex-executive at Chinese state power firm Datang given suspended death sentence, state media says\" [ref=e32]:\n          - /url: /world/china/ex-executive-chinese-state-power-firm-datang-given-suspended-death-sentence-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: Kou Wei, a former senior executive at a major Chinese state-owned ‌power-generating company, was sentenced to death with a two-year reprieve over crimes including taking bribes, state news ⁠agency Xinhua reported on Wednesday.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Sustainability category\" [ref=e33] [nth=1]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 14 hours ago\n        - link \"Bank of England says Iran war has boosted threats to financial stability\" [ref=e34]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/boards-policy-regulation/bank-england-says-iran-war-has-boosted-threats-financial-stability-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: By David Milliken and Phoebe Seers\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e35] [nth=2]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 14 hours ago\n        - link \"Chinese chipmakers claim nearly half of local market as Nvidia's lead shrinks, includes gallery\" [ref=e36]:\n          - /url: /world/china/chinese-chipmakers-claim-nearly-half-of-local-market-nvidias-lead-shrinks-idc-2026-04-01/\n          - text: Chinese chipmakers claim nearly half of local market as Nvidia's lead shrinks\n        - paragraph: Chinese GPU and AI chip ‌makers captured nearly 41% of China's AI accelerator server market last year, eroding Nvidia's once-dominant position in one of its most important overseas markets, according to data from an IDC report reviewed by Reuters.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Sustainability category\" [ref=e37] [nth=2]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 13 hours ago\n        - link \"EU fines on US companies are biggest source of friction, State Department official says\" [ref=e38] [nth=1]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/boards-policy-regulation/eu-fines-us-companies-are-biggest-source-friction-state-department-official-says-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: A senior U.S. State Department official said on Wednesday that European Union fines on U.S. companies are the biggest source of friction in transatlantic economic relations, singling out the bloc's Digital ⁠Markets Act, which targets dominant tech platforms.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Business category\" [ref=e39] [nth=2]:\n          - /url: /business/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 13 hours ago\n          - /url: /business/finance/global-markets-view-usa-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: What matters in U.S. and global markets today\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Business category\" [ref=e40] [nth=3]:\n          - /url: /business/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 13 hours ago\n        - link \"Russia exports more LNG in first quarter, shipments to Europe jump too, data shows\" [ref=e41] [nth=1]:\n          - /url: /business/energy/russia-exports-more-lng-first-quarter-shipments-europe-jump-too-data-shows-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: Russia exported more liquefied natural gas in the first quarter of 2026 than it did a year earlier, with shipments to Europe increasing despite Moscow's push to redirect supply away from the ‌region.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Sustainability category\" [ref=e42] [nth=3]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/\n  