istitem:\n        - link \"Sustainability category\" [ref=e54] [nth=5]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 18 hours ago\n        - link \"EU lawmakers press China on unsafe products on rare Beijing visit, includes gallery\" [ref=e55]:\n          - /url: /sustainability/society-equity/eu-lawmakers-press-china-unsafe-products-rare-beijing-visit-2026-04-01/\n          - text: EU lawmakers press China on unsafe products on rare Beijing visit\n        - paragraph: EU lawmakers this week pressed China over a ‌surge of dangerous products into the bloc and insufficient access to the Chinese market as they kicked off the first European parliamentary visit to the world's No.2 economy in eight years.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e56] [nth=6]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 16 hours ago\n        - link \"World does not need a crisis over Taiwan, opposition leader says ahead of China trip, includes gallery\" [ref=e57]:\n          - /url: /world/china/world-does-not-need-crisis-over-taiwan-opposition-leader-says-ahead-china-trip-2026-04-01/\n          - text: World does not need a crisis over Taiwan, opposition leader says ahead of China trip\n        - paragraph: At a time of international turbulence the world does not need a crisis over Taiwan, the leader ‌of the island's largest opposition party said on Wednesday ahead of a trip to China, adding she is seeking reconciliation.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e58] [nth=7]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 20 hours ago\n        - link \"China's new home prices rise in March; big cities see seasonal pickup, private survey shows\" [ref=e59]:\n          - /url: /world/china/chinas-new-home-prices-rise-march-big-cities-see-seasonal-pickup-private-survey-2026-04-01/\n        - paragraph: China's new home prices edged up in March, reversing a decline in the previous month, supported by a seasonal pickup in demand in major cities, a private survey ‌showed on Wednesday.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e60] [nth=8]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 12 hours ago\n        - link \"Factory input costs soar worldwide as Iran war snarls up supply chains, includes gallery\" [ref=e61]:\n          - /url: /world/china/global-economy-asias-factory-activity-slows-cost-pressure-iran-war-2026-04-01/\n          - text: Factory input costs soar worldwide as Iran war snarls up supply chains\n        - paragraph: Factories across the world faced soaring input costs and supply chain disruptions in March due to the Iran war as underlying tepid demand threatened to undermine the manufacturing sector's fragile recovery, surveys showed.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Asia Pacific category\" [ref=e62]:\n          - /url: /world/asia-pacific/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: March 31, 2026\n        - link \"China factories log fastest growth in a year as war risks loom large, includes gallery\" [ref=e63]:\n          - /url: /world/asia-pacific/chinas-factory-activity-returns-expansion-pmi-shows-2026-03-31/\n          - text: China factories log fastest growth in a year as war risks loom large\n        - paragraph: China's factory activity grew at the fastest pace in a year in March, underpinned by improved demand, an official survey showed on Tuesday, a welcome relief for an economy grappling with global ‌supply chain strains and energy market volatility.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e64] [nth=9]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: March 31, 2026\n        - link \"China's top airlines cautious on outlook as Iran war raises fuel costs\" [ref=e65]:\n          - /url: /world/china/chinas-top-airlines-cautious-outlook-iran-war-raises-fuel-costs-2026-03-31/\n        - paragraph: China's three largest state-owned airlines said they were cautious about the outlook for this year as the Iran war drives jet fuel prices sky-high, after all returned to losses in the fourth quarter of 2025.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Business category\" [ref=e66] [nth=4]:\n          - /url: /business/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 23 hours ago\n        - link \"Republican senator proposes to widen US ban on Chinese autos\" [ref=e67]:\n          - /url: /business/autos-transportation/republican-senator-proposes-widen-us-ban-chinese-autos-2026-03-31/\n        - paragraph: Republican Senator Bernie Moreno said ‌on Tuesday he will introduce legislation next month to toughen a U.S. government ban on Chinese automakers from entering the American market, and encouraged other countries to follow suit.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Business category\" [ref=e68] [nth=5]:\n          - /url: /business/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 15 hours ago\n        - link \"Nike forecasts surprise sales drop as China weakness hurts turnaround efforts, includes video\" [ref=e69]:\n          - /url: /business/retail-consumer/nike-third-quarter-sales-beat-estimates-2026-03-31/\n          - text: Nike forecasts surprise sales drop as China weakness hurts turnaround efforts\n        - paragraph: Nike's forecast of a surprise drop in fourth-quarter sales on Tuesday sent its shares down more than 9% in extended trading, as persistent ‌weakness in China and slow progress in clearing older inventory hamper turnaround efforts.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Asia Pacific category\" [ref=e70] [nth=1]:\n          - /url: /world/asia-pacific/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 7 hours ago\n        - link \"Japan, France agree rare earths deal to cut China reliance, NHK reports\" [ref=e71]:\n          - /url: /world/asia-pacific/japan-france-ink-rare-earths-deal-nikkei-reports-2026-03-31/\n        - paragraph: Japan and France agreed to strengthen support for rare earths supply chains on Wednesday, Japan's public ‌broadcaster NHK reported, in the latest moves by both countries to lessen dependence on the world's dominant supplier, China.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e72] [nth=10]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: March 31, 2026\n        - link \"Mongolia names new prime minister following stalemate in parliament\" [ref=e73]:\n          - /url: /world/china/mongolia-names-new-prime-minister-following-stalemate-parliament-2026-03-31/\n        - paragraph: Mongolia's parliament on Monday confirmed Uchral Nyam-Osor as the nation's third prime minister in nine months, following his predecessor's resignation last week over strife within the ruling Mongolian People’s Party and a legislative stalemate.\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"China category\" [ref=e74] [nth=11]:\n          - /url: /world/china/\n        - text: ·\n        - time: 22 hours ago\n        - link \"China, Pakistan call for Iran peace talks, normal navigation in Strait of Hormuz, includes gallery\" [ref=e75]:\n          - /url: /world/china/china-pakistan-call-start-peace-talks-soon-possible-state-media-reports-2026-03-31/\n          - text: China, Pakistan call for Iran peace talks, normal navigation in Strait of Hormuz\n        - paragraph: China and Pakistan on Tuesday called for an immediate ceasefire in the Gulf and the wider Middle East, urging the swift launch of ‌peace talks and the restoration of normal navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, as their foreign ministers met in Beijing.\n    - button \"Load more articles\" [ref=e76]\n  - contentinfo:\n    - heading \"Site Index\" [ref=e77] [level=3]\n    - heading \"Latest\" [ref=e78] [level=3]\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Home\" [ref=e79]:\n          - /url: /\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Authors\" [ref=e80]:\n          - /url: /sitemap/authors/\n      - listitem:\n        - link \"Topic Sitemap\" [ref=e81]:\n          - /url: /sitemap/topics/\n      - listitem:\n        - link