[x] Collected Reuters China news for April 2, 2026 (13 stories: China chip market 41% share, Iran war impact, Taiwan opposition leader visit, housing prices, Nike China decline, US-China car restrictions, China-Pakistan peace call, France Navy comment, EU Beijing visit, Datang Power corruption, Cambodia extradition, NASA moon mission)\n- [x] Collected Lianhe Zaobao China news for April 2, 2026 (~20 stories: Guangxi taxi incident, Chinese student Italy, Li Qiang Sichuan, Xi-Zheng meeting analysis, Taiwan movies labeled, Trump Iran, Russia-China railway, Canada FM visit, Hong Kong LegCo election, etc.)\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] **monifeixing → 下载管理** robocopy (session `quick-gulf`, ~10GB+ Flight Simulator content, files progressing through asobo-*.fspackage, still running)\n- [ ] **x300pro → 手机备份** robocopy (session `nimble-wharf`, ~1GB+ vivo photo backup, still running)\n- [ ] **Remaining small folders to move** (13 folders mapped via index, blocked by encoding issues; to be retried after large transfers complete):\n  - 学习资料: 作业, 习题, 教育培训, 工程项目建议学院\n  - 视频剪辑: 影片视频剪辑, vi乱码, 电影相关, 电影4K原版, 一生一世\n  - 下载管理: idm乱码\n  - 文档工具: 文档, sa, 备份\n- [ ] **F:\\电子书 reorganization** (71 files into 9 category subfolders, pending)\n\n### Blocked\n- [x] Z-Library ebook automation: cancelled by user; blocked by anti-bot measures and browser download routing limitations\n- [x] Chinese folder name encoding: workaround found (Python index-based access), but script stuck on robocopy calls — retried after large transfers complete\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Gateway fix**: Added 10-second `timeout /t 10 /nobreak >nul` to gateway.cmd before gateway launches\n- **F盘 reorganization**: Categories by usage/purpose; u-claw kept as-is under 文档工具; x300pro = phone photo backup → 手机备份\n- **Z-Library downloads**: Not automated; user cancelled task\n- **Daily Reuters news**: Windows schtasks scheduled task instead of cron; script saves to file for agent to deliver on next interaction\n- **Chinese folder encoding workaround**: Use Python index-based `os.listdir()` access to avoid hardcoding garbled Chinese characters in scripts\n- **Large folder transfers prioritized**: monifeixing (~10GB+) and x300pro (~1GB+) run in background first; smaller folders queued after\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Wait for background robocopy sessions `quick-gulf` (monifeixing) and `nimble-wharf` (x300pro) to complete\n2. Retry Python script `C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\scripts\\move_folders.py` to move remaining 13 small folders\n3. Delete empty folders after all moves complete (Podcasts, 新建文件夹, Alarms, 电影文件夹, Download, WeGameApps, Audiobooks)\n4. Delete empty source folders after robocopy completes\n5. **F:\\电子书 reorganization**: create 9 category subfolders, move 71 ebook files\n6. Monitor daily news collection (Reuters at 7:30 AM via scheduled task)\n\n## Critical Context\n- **F盘 folder stats** (from recursive count):\n  - u-claw: 48,157 files | monifeixing: 10,807 files | idm乱码: 10,159 files | 影片视频剪辑: 6,222 files | 工程项目建议学院: 2,327 files | BaiduNetdiskDownload: 1,863 files | x300pro: 1,058 files | 乱码: 523 files | 作业: 391 files | 教育培训: 326 files | vi乱码: 325 files | 游戏: 71 files | 文档: 67 files | 硬盘: 24 files | sa: 21 files | 备份: 7 files | 习题: 5 files\n- **Robocopy sessions**: `quick-gulf` (monifeixing→下载管理), `nimble-wharf` (x300pro→手机备份) — both still running\n- **Reuters cron task**: `OpenClaw_ReutersNews`, scheduled 2026/04/03 7:30 AM, script `C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\scripts\\fetch_reuters.ps1`\n- **Ebooks to organize in F:\\电子书** (71 files): 历史(14), 世界文学(4), 心理学社科(12), 财经商业(2), 艺术设计(16), 政治党史(19), 碑帖书法(1), 食谱(1), 日本文化(2)\n- **move_folders.py** at `C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\scripts\\move_folders.py` — uses index-based folder access (indices 2,3,4,5,6,8,9,10,11,12,14,22,29 from `os.listdir('F:\\\\')`), retried after large transfers complete\n- **Reuters news April 2, 2026**: 13 China stories (chip sector, Iran war, Taiwan, housing, Nike, US-China auto, geopolitics, corruption)\n- **Lianhe Zaobao news April 2, 2026**: ~20 China stories (taxi incident, Xi-Zheng meeting, Trump Iran, Russia-China railway, HK LegCo, etc.)\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nUser wants to collect/harvest public exam (公考) related content from Douyin (TikTok China) to see what oral broadcast (口播) content they could create recently.\n\n## Early Progress\n1. Attempted `web_search` twice but got \"count must be <= 10\" validation errors, then \"fetch failed\"\n2. Tried browsing Douyin directly - requires login, couldn't access content\n3. Tried browsing Toutiao video search - page didn't render search results\n4. Tried browsing Weibo video search - requires login\n5. Tried `web_fetch` on 澎湃新闻 (The Paper) - search redirected to homepage, no useful results\n6. Tried browsing Bilibili - page didn't load search results (logged-out view)\n7. Finally navigated to Baidu to search for \"公考面试必考热点2026\" (public exam interview must-know hot topics 2026)\n\n## Context for Suffix\nThe assistant is currently on a Baidu search results page waiting for the snapshot. The snapshot was truncated at 161K+ characters but shows only navigation elements so far. The actual search results content (which would contain the hot topics the user requested) was cut off by the truncation.\n\n<read-files>\nC:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\ClawX\\resources\\openclaw\\skills\\tavily-search\\SKILL.md\n</read-files>","firstKeptEntryId":"321c688f","tokensBefore":194121,"details":{"readFiles":["C:\\Users\\zhang\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\ClawX\\resources\\openclaw\\skills\\tavily-search\\SKILL.md"],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
