{"type":"message","id":"c570213d","parentId":"401ea269","timestamp":"2026-04-02T06:42:47.240Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to collect all the images from Behance and save them to a separate folder. Let me think about how to do this.\n\nFrom what I've seen in the Behance pages, the images are project covers/thumbnails. I can try to extract image URLs from the pages and download them.\n\nHowever, looking at the browser snapshots, I don't see direct image URLs in the text content. The images are embedded in the page via JavaScript rendering. \n\nLet me try to:\n1. Create a folder for the collected images\n2. Try to extract image URLs from the Behance pages\n3. Download them using curl or similar tools\n\nActually, the browser snapshots don't show the image URLs - they're just referenced as elements. I'd need to either:\n1. Use browser automation to right-click and save images\n2. Try to find the image URLs from the page source\n3. Use web_fetch to get the page HTML and extract image URLs\n\nLet me try to fetch the page and extract images. But this might be complex since Behance loads images dynamically.\n\nAlternatively, I could navigate to each project page and try to download the cover images from there.\n\nLet me create a folder first, then try to extract and download images from the Behance pages I've already collected.","thinkingSignature":"4f25e95638da3625a9a6de338a66de86b41c886ea8c08d7f50ccf5eef98c8a3d"},{"type":"text","text":"好的，我来帮你采集Behance的图片！先创建一个文件夹：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_57hnkfja48d8_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p \"C:\\Users\\zhang\\.openclaw\\workspace\\Behance_Trends_2026\" 2>$null; echo \"Folder created\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":127,"output":341,"cacheRead":89972,"cacheWrite":8532,"totalTokens":98972,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":